collapsed before scoring. Copies posted in the same minute that the parser did not recognise remain in the sample (counts in the robustness block).","A post is scored once per contract. The channel's own quoted entry is shown only to test whether it could have been filled.","Only public channels are scored. Parsing is automatic and can be wrong."],"limitations":["Bars are trade prints, not bid and ask. Spread and slippage are NOT modelled, so true results for someone trading these calls would be worse, most of all on wide-spread, low-priced contracts.","Option bars come from an indicative data feed; some venues or prints may be missing and a bar's open may differ from what was available at the second of the post. A one-off comparison against archived Yahoo daily bars (311 contract-days) found closes matched in 95%, lows in 78% and highs in only 55%, with the feed's high above Yahoo's in 110 cases (33 by more than 10%). Peaks and TP-first are therefore upper-leaning (part of the gap may be partial-day capture in the reference).","The fill is the open of the first 5-minute bar starting at or after the post, so the bar containing the post is skipped: the median gap from post to that bar is about 2.5 minutes (90th percentile about 4.6 minutes, see fill_gap). The 0-minute row is therefore not an instant fill, and every delay row is that much later still.","The quoted-entry comparison is between the channel's quote and the fill price after that gap, not the price at the second of the post.","Statistical ranges (Wilson) treat calls as independent. They are not: calls cluster on a few days, tickers (SPX) and channels, and some copies of the same contract remain. Day-clustered ranges in the robustness block are wider and are the better guide.","The 30-minute window is short by design. It describes what happened right after a call, not what a different exit rule or a longer hold would have done.","A same-bar tie between the take-profit and stop-loss levels counts as the stop, which is conservative; the true order inside a 5-minute bar is unknown.","A quoted entry far below the contract's traded price at the post could not have been filled; those are counted and shown rather than removed.","The sample covers a limited date range and a few busy channels; rates describe this sample and are not settled estimates.","Calls with no bars, thin trading or an illiquid first print are excluded from the scored sample (see the coverage funnel). Contracts that never traded or opened illiquid are plausibly the worst outcomes, so the exclusion probably flatters the result.","Some windows end early (the contract stopped printing) and some rest on 2 or fewer bars; where neither level is hit the position is valued at the last print, which can be stale. Counts are in the robustness block.","Not advice. Flagged for investigation, not a finding of fraud."]},"window_start":"2026-03-26","window_end":"2026-10-14","small_n_threshold":25,"coverage":{"stages":[{"stage":"Option open callouts (repeat posts removed)","n":3508},{"stage":"With a parseable contract (ticker, side, strike, expiry)","n":2846},{"stage":"No bars for the evaluation window (not captured, not listed, or no trades)","n":98},{"stage":"Unscorable (see reasons)","n":11},{"stage":"Coarse day view only (no 5-minute bars; not in the headline)","n":10},{"stage":"Scored from 5-minute bars","n":2727},{"stage":"  of which intraday (30-minute window)","n":2696},{"stage":"  of which daily callout (whole next session)","n":31}],"unscorable_by_reason":[{"reason":"illiquid: first print more than 15 minutes after the post or the open","n":11}],"no_bars_by_category":{"unknown":74,"intraday":23,"daily":1},"status_counts":{"scored":2727,"unscorable":11,"no_bars":98,"day_view":10},"no_bars_unknown_note":"'unknown' = the contract was not captured at all (older than the data retains, or not listed), so the call was never placed in the intraday or daily window."},"pooled":{"intraday":{"n":2696,"ended_green":{"k":975,"